# What must NOT go into the Docker build context.
#
# app/Dockerfile does `COPY crdt-core/ crdt-core/` and `COPY app/ app/`, and frontend/Dockerfile
# does `COPY . .` — so without this file a local `target/` (tens of megabytes of class files and
# jars) and a local `node_modules/` were shipped to the daemon on every build and then copied into
# a layer, where the build immediately overwrote them with its own.
#
# Two costs, and the second is the one that bites: a slow build, and an image whose contents depend
# on what happens to be lying around in the working directory. `npm ci` and `mvn package` are
# supposed to make the build reproducible; a stale directory smuggled in through the context
# quietly undoes that.

# Build output
target/
**/target/
dist/
**/dist/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Version control and CI
.git/
.github/

# Local tooling and editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
.DS_Store

# Test and demo artefacts
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
frontend/demo-recordings/
crdt-core/.jqwik-database

# Local environment
.env
.env.local
*.local.yml
